#: Behler.md:99
msgid ""
"The code is faster if the calculations that are done with CUSTOM keywords in"
" the input above are implemented directly in C++. Even so the fact that you "
"can so quickly prototype complicated CVs like these is (I hope) useful."
msgstr "CUSTOM 部分を直接 C++ にすれば速くなりますが、複雑な CV の迅速な試作も有用だと思います。"

#: Behler.md:102
msgid "Implementing angular symmetry functionsa"
msgstr "Angular Symmetry Function の実装"

#: Behler.md:104
msgid "One of the angular symmetry functions that Behler introduces is:"
msgstr "Behler の Angular Function の1つは、"

#: Behler.md:110
msgid ""
"In this expression $\\zeta$, $\\nu$ and $\\lambda$ are all parameters. $f_c$"
" is a switching function which acts upon $R_{ij}$, the distance between atom"
" $i$ and atom $j$, and $R_{ik}$, the distance between atom $i$ and atom $k$."
" $\\theta_{ijk}$ is then the angle between the vector that points from atom "
"$i$ to atom $j$ and the vector that points from atom $i$ to atom $k$."
msgstr ""
"$\\zeta$、$\\nu$、$\\lambda$ はパラメータです。$f_c$ は原子 $i$・$j$ の距離 $R_{ij}$ と、原子 "
"$i$・$k$ の距離 $R_{ik}$ に作用します。$\\theta_{ijk}$ は原子 $i$ から $j$、原子 $i$ から $k$ の "
"Vector 間角です。"

#: Behler.md:114
msgid ""
"Even this complicated function can be calculated directly in PLUMED. The "
"input below caluclates the $G^5_i$ value for atom 1 with $\\zeta=3$, "
"$\\lambda=3$ and $\\nu=0.1$."
msgstr "これも直接計算できます。次は原子1の $G^5_i$ を $\\zeta=3$、$\\lambda=3$、$\\nu=0.1$ で求めます。"

#: Behler.md:153
msgid ""
"This input computes $G^5$ for a single atom and is rather cumbersome. The "
"calculation here is not particularly well optimised as we have to calculate "
"the distance between atom 1 and all the other atoms. In other words, when an"
" input similar to this one is used PLUMED is not using link cells or "
"neighbour lists to optimse the calculation. This way of implementing $G^5$ "
"is thus not really suited to production applications. I thus wrote a second "
"implementation of the $G^5$ function. The input for this alternative "
"implementation is as follows:"
msgstr ""
"単一原子の $G^5$ には煩雑で、全原子との距離を計算し、Link Cells・Neighbor List も使わないため本計算には不向きです。別の "
"$G^5$ 実装を用意しました。$G^5$ の別版の入力は、"

#: Behler.md:177
msgid ""
"The GSYMFUNC_THREEBODY action sums over all the distinct triples of atoms "
"that are identified in the contact matrix. This action auses lepton and can "
"thus compute any function of the following four quantities:"
msgstr ""
"GSYMFUNC_THREEBODY は Contact Matrix 内の異なる全3原子組を足し合わせます。Lepton "
"で次の4量の任意関数を計算できます。"

#: Behler.md:180
msgid "`rij` - the distance between atom $i$ and atom $j$"
msgstr "`rij`：原子 $i$ と $j$ の距離。"

#: Behler.md:181
msgid "`rik` - the distance between atom $i$ and atom $k$"
msgstr "`rik`：原子 $i$ と $k$ の距離。"

#: Behler.md:182
msgid "`rjk` - the distance between atom $j$ and atom $k$"
msgstr "`rjk`：原子 $j$ と $k$ の距離。"

#: Behler.md:183
msgid ""
"`ajik` - the angle between the vector connecting atom $i$ to atom $j$ and "
"the vector connecting atom $i$ to atom $k$."
msgstr "`ajik`：原子 $i$ から $j$ と、原子 $i$ から $k$ の Vector 間角。"

#: Behler.md:185
msgid ""
"Furthermore we can calculate more than one function of these four quantities"
" at a time as illustrated by the input below:"
msgstr "同時に複数の関数も計算できます。"

#: Behler.md:209
msgid ""
"As we saw for the radial symmetry function, we thus again have an "
"implementation of these angular symmetry functions that can be quickly used "
"to prototype new function types."
msgstr "Radial の場合と同様、新しい Angular Function を迅速に試作できます。"

#: Behler.md:211
msgid "Conclusions"
msgstr "結論"

#: Behler.md:213
msgid ""
"I hope the examples above have convinced you that the PLUMED input file now "
"provides the flexibility required to prototype CVs that are really rather "
"complicated. Using CUSTOM actions when implementing these CVs is probably "
"not optimal when it comes to computational performance but I am not "
"convinced that this matters. I think our objective should always be to have "
"less code as this makes PLUMED easier to maintain."
msgstr ""
"入力だけで非常に複雑な CV を試作できる柔軟性が伝われば幸いです。CUSTOM "
"は性能上最適とは限りませんが、それほど重要とは思いません。コードを減らし保守を容易にすることを目指すべきだと考えます。"

#: Behler.md:217
msgid ""
"It is also the case that many of the CVs that are implemented in PLUMED are "
"not used by many people. The understanding of what particular actions do is "
"thus lost with time. When CVs are implemented in the way above the series of"
" action that are performed within them are more transparent. This "
"transparency allows allows other to understand what has been done in the "
"past and reduces the requirements to write large amounts of documentation."
msgstr ""
"多くの CV は利用者が少なく、何をする Action "
"かの理解が時間とともに失われます。この方式なら処理の系列が透明で、過去の実装を理解しやすく、膨大な文書の必要性も減ります。"

#: Behler.md:221
msgid ""
"Lastly, if users need code that runs faster they can always reimplement "
"expensive CVs that are implemented in PLUMED. Furthermore, in any effort to "
"reimplement CVs they are helped by the fact that PLUMED offers reference "
"values that they can test their new code against."
msgstr "高速化が必要なら高コスト CV を再実装できます。PLUMED の参照値で新コードを検証できることも助けになります。"
